I can explain the exploit, at least. (I'm not sure on the other points
in your post.)

The idea is that level gain via failed polyself ("You feel like a new
man/woman/race!") uses a different formula than regular level
gain/drain; if you change to double your current level, it gives you
double your HP and Pw. So you level-drain to 1 (losing a fixed amount
of HP per level), then failed-polyself to a higher level (gaining an
amount of HP proportional to the amount you already had). If you have
an above-average amount of HP to start with, repeating this gives an
exponential HP growth.

Note that failed polyself at level 1 has a moderatly high chance of
killing you. As a result, this exploit requires many amulets of life
saving to pull off, normally obtained via pudding farming.

